# 📦 PROJECT VISION & SCOPE

We are building a cross-platform real-time AI desktop engine running natively on macOS, Windows, and Linux.

The application must be designed to operate across a wide range of hardware configurations, from lower-powered development/compatibility systems to high-performance systems with dedicated GPUs.

The software processes live camera and microphone streams through local AI models and outputs the result to system Virtual Camera and Virtual Microphone drivers compatible with Telegram, Zoom, WhatsApp, Discord, OBS, Google Meet, and similar applications.

The application must NOT assume that every supported computer has a dedicated gaming GPU.

The engine must detect the available hardware and automatically select appropriate processing paths, AI models, resolution, processing frequency, and optional features according to the capabilities of the current system.

## Key Features (All AI Inference Local)

1. **Realistic Real-Time Face Swap:** Sub-15ms identity replacement target on appropriate hardware.
2. **Real-Time Voice Conversion (RVC):** Pitch extraction and voice timbre conversion with <40ms audio latency target on appropriate hardware.
3. **User Voice Upload & Voice Profile Creation:** The user must be able to upload an audio file or video containing a voice, extract/process the usable voice data, and create a reusable voice profile/model for real-time conversion.
4. **Saved Voice Library:** Users must be able to create, name, save, select, update, and delete multiple voice profiles.
5. **Voice Storage & Synchronization:** Voice source assets, generated voice-model assets, and voice metadata must be stored and synchronized through Firebase where appropriate. Large binary assets must use Firebase Storage rather than being stored directly inside Firestore documents.
6. **Local Voice Model Cache:** Voice models/assets downloaded from Firebase must be cached locally so real-time calls do not depend on Firebase network access or downloading a model during a live call.
7. **Pre-Call Voice Configuration:** Before starting a call, the user must be able to select a saved voice, load/verify the required local model, configure available voice settings, and confirm that the voice is ready.
8. **Voice Preview/Test:** The user must be able to test the selected voice with the live microphone before starting a call and hear the converted result.
9. **Real-Time Voice Routing:** During a call, the user's live microphone audio must be processed through the selected voice conversion pipeline and routed to the system Virtual Microphone.
10. **Lip Sync & Facial Animation:** Real-time mouth mesh deformation matching the processed/cloned audio.
11. **Body Movement & Garment Overlay:** Computer vision skeletal tracking and real-time clothing texture mapping.
12. **Background Matting & Sky Blending:** Real-time subject segmentation, background replacement, and environmental lighting color-matching.
13. **Virtual Driver Routing:** System-level Virtual Cam (DirectShow/CMIO/v4l2loopback) & Virtual Mic (WASAPI/CoreAudio/PipeWire).
14. **Firebase Integration:** Firebase C++ SDK integration for authentication, user profiles, voice metadata, voice/preset synchronization, configuration, and telemetry where appropriate.

