# 🗣️ VOICE PROFILE & REAL-TIME VOICE WORKFLOW

The voice system must create a reusable voice profile/model from user-provided source material.

The uploaded source may be:

* An audio file.
* A video file containing speech.
* Other supported media formats introduced by later milestones.

The uploaded recording must NOT simply be played back during the call.

The purpose is to allow the user to speak new words naturally while the real-time conversion system produces the selected voice characteristics.

## Voice Workflow Requirement

The intended voice workflow is:

```text
User uploads audio/video
        ↓
Extract voice/audio
        ↓
Validate source
        ↓
Voice preprocessing
        ↓
Create / prepare voice profile or model
        ↓
Save voice metadata + assets
        ↓
Firebase Storage / Firestore
        ↓
Local model cache
        ↓
User selects voice before call
        ↓
Load and verify local voice model
        ↓
Configure voice settings
        ↓
Microphone test / voice preview
        ↓
User confirms voice is ready
        ↓
Start call
        ↓
Live microphone
        ↓
Pitch extraction + RVC conversion
        ↓
Selected voice
        ↓
Virtual Microphone
        ↓
Telegram / WhatsApp / Discord / Zoom / etc.
```

The application must support multiple saved voice profiles rather than assuming only one voice.

Voice preparation/model loading that can be performed before the call must happen before the call whenever practical.

Do not introduce avoidable model preparation, downloads, or heavy initialization into the real-time call path.

